Subject: [PATCH] fix(re-exec-portal): remove orphaned dead guide-widget markup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Removes leftover 'DYNAMIC INTERACTIVE GUIDE FOR EU' block: its outer
wrapper, header, and step-1 section were already missing (truncated
in a past edit), leaving unwrapped exec-step-2/3 divs plus a stray
</div> that broke div-balance for the rest of the page. Its click
listener also called an undefined markComplete() (real function was
named completeStep), so it never worked even before the truncation.
The fully working 'GUIDE · EXEC PORTAL DECISIONING' widget (sg-step-*
ids) already covers this exact use case with cleaner copy, so this is
dead code, not a feature to reconstruct.

Verified: all 28 <script> blocks pass node --check; div-tag balance
is clean (depth never goes negative) across the whole file.
---
 html/war-rooms/re-war/re-exec-portal.html | 79 -----------------------
 1 file changed, 79 deletions(-)

